plan.what_it_does:
Checked against HEAD. `git diff 9cb92b1 HEAD -- backend/app/trace/quotes.py backend/app/trace/bind.py` is empty, so the binder evaluated in the main run is the production binder.

ENTRY POINT. resolve_case_trace (bind.py:43-85):
- Builds a registry from the case sources plus answered follow-ups, which enter as QA-nn sources (bind.py:28-40, 49-50).
- Drops repeated claim_ids and keeps the first (bind.py:88-96).
- Resolves every claim (bind.py:191-214).

PER CITATION (resolved_citations, bind.py:254-281):
- A citation whose source_id is not in the registry is dropped (264-266).
- The quote goes through located_quote (bind.py:232-236):
  - it first strips a leading or trailing ellipsis (quotes.py:10, 163-165);
  - it accepts the quote if it occurs ANYWHERE, even more than once (bind.py:235);
  - otherwise it calls find_aligned_quote;
  - it rejects a result longer than 2,000 characters (quotes.py:8).
- find_aligned_quote tries these tiers in order, and each accepts only a UNIQUE match (quotes.py:168-213):
  1. exact (172-176);
  2. NFKC fold with an index map back to the source (216-228);
  3. ellipsis expansion (231-260);
  4. a regex that tolerates markup and quote marks: it strips *_#`~, lets any quote mark match any other (11, 186-199), allows whitespace or nothing between characters of a word and between words (199, 202), and is case-sensitive.
- The accepted quote is REPLACED by the source span (270-276). A reader therefore only ever sees source text.
- Duplicate (source, quote) pairs are collapsed (277-280).
- A document/page locator is set only when it is unique (quotes.py:53-72, 91-119).

STATUS RULE. A claim with epistemic_status "reported" and no surviving supporting citation becomes "not_confirmed" (bind.py:217-220). The other statuses are never checked (claims.py:18-25).

REFERENCES:
- claim_ids on parties, timeline and impacts are filtered to known claims (bind.py:99-102).
- A gap's affected_claim_ids are filtered, and askable is forced false for EXPLICITLY_UNKNOWN (105-111).
- supporting and contradicting source ids are filtered to the registry (223-229).
- An ATT&CK association is dropped when (bind.py:114-138):
  - no retrieval happened;
  - the id does not fullmatch T\d{4}(\.\d{3})? (bind.py:25);
  - the technique is not in the retrieved mitre_table;
  - or no known claim is left on it.
- Items left with no claim_ids are KEPT.
- The summary text is never checked.

COUNTS. grounding_report (bind.py:141-188, fields at trace.py:89-103) stores:
- claims, and citations claimed, verified, paraphrased and unfound;
- claims without a citation, duplicated claims and citations;
- the two association drop counts;
- sources cited and total.

Paraphrase is diagnostic only: a failed quote sharing at least 60% of its character trigrams is counted as "paraphrased" and never accepted (quotes.py:9, 46-50; bind.py:170-171).

NOT COUNTED:
- dropped claim references, which have no field;
- citations dropped before binding by normalized_citation for an empty or over-long quote (claims.py:185-199).

NOT CHECKED: whether a quote supports its claim. related_studies_modules.md says the same.

verdict.corrected_plan_summary:
COMPONENT: the binder at HEAD, identical to 9cb92b1, which the main run used (summary.json commit 9cb92b1, no tracked changes). What it does is as the plan describes, with every line citation checked. Add: (a) role_source_ids keeps model-named source ids after a failed quote (bind.py:223-229), and the report falls back to them (display.py:197-198); (b) the grounding report has no field for dropped claim references, and it reports a collapsed trace (case 132) as perfect.

QUESTIONS: Q1-Q6 and Q8 as proposed. Q7 is reworded as 'stable across writer configurations' (gemma two-call main; gemma one-call single and single_late; deepseek one-call case_direct RQ2), with confounds named. Add Q9: does a claim with no verified quote still carry a source label in the report?

BASELINES (all free, same inputs):
- no binder;
- exact substring only (804 or 803 by convention, 64 downgrades);
- production (860 located / 859 kept, 9 downgrades);
- production + edge quote-mark strip (864/869, 5), labelled exploratory because it was derived in-sample;
- whole-document trigram >= 0.6 ceiling (869, 0), labelled a diagnostic ceiling, not a published baseline;
- optionally a sliding-window edit-distance variant.
One verbatim-rate definition is used throughout (harness-published 0.988 = kept/claimed, or 0.990 located/claimed; state which).

METRICS (judge-free):
- verbatim rate;
- citation coverage (Zhang stage 1, preprint);
- per-tier share, with the attribution convention stated;
- false-rejection rate (ours, pre-registered, with a punctuation-sensitive variant; 4/869 = 0.46%, Wilson [0.18%, 1.18%]);
- relaxed-tier drift (0/54) plus the perturbation suite (frozen now; cite metamorphic testing, doi:10.1145/3143561, or CheckList, doi:10.18653/v1/2020.acl-main.442, not mutation testing);
- status downgrades per writer configuration (Murzaku only as framing);
- dangling references per trace (1/48) with the root cause;
- unverified-source-label count (9/9);
- misleading-verbatim candidate rates as diagnostics only (NegEx, BioScope; Windisch's support rate is LLM-judged).

